libvips builds its command line tools, its test programs and its fuzzers as part of `all`, with no
option to turn any of them off. Against a static dependency stack that is around nineteen
executables, each linking the whole of libvips and everything beneath it -- the four tools alone are
19MB apiece -- and nothing here runs them.

Upstream strips these same three lines with a regexp for its oss-fuzz builds, per the comment above
them, so this is a seam it already expects to be cut.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -778,6 +778,3 @@
 # these lines removed by a regexp for oss-fuzz builds, don't touch!
 subdir('man')
 subdir('po')
-subdir('tools')
-subdir('test')
-subdir('fuzz')
